<title>UK: Regalian to pay H1 dividend as sales boom.</title>
<headline>Regalian to pay H1 dividend as sales boom.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.39		   vs 0.38</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.4		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax		     1.62		   vs 0.44</p>
<p> Turnover		   11.12		  vs 2.99</p>
<p> Operating result	 1.83		   vs 0.61</p>
<p> Associates result loss 0.36		   vs 0.29</p>
<p> Interest income	  0.15		   vs 0.12</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.62		   vs 0.44</p>
<p> Retained		   1.16		   vs 0.44</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 17</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 26</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Regalian Properties, which announced a rights issue alongside its results, said that trading had remained buoyant since the end of the reported period with new reservations already achieved amounting to 21.8 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
